Error [jet.UninitializedRead]: `x` may be read before it is given a value
  --> tests/ui/uninit_read_before_write.jet:6:11
    |
  6 |     print(x)
    |           ^
 Why: `x` was declared with `Type{ uninit }`, so no value is available until you write to it — this read could see garbage
 Fix: Assign `x` on every path before reading it; a fixed list needs every slot assigned
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E0420
